        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-12T05:35:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And suddenly, OblivAeon reminds me a lot of the big bad from Worm (whose name I won't mention, because spoilers), who is similarly singular across alternate timelines. &nbsp;(And dealt with by a similar gathering of cross dimensional heros and villains)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Ahem… that character is ALSO something of a reference to OblivAeon's most direct inspiration, the Anti-Monitor.&nbsp; Ever since Crisis on Infite Earths, multiverally singular genocidal beings are all the rage.&nbsp; Transformers has one, even new Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles went that route for their version of Shredder.&nbsp; DC and Marvel themselves have both gone back to that well <em>within the past year</em>.&nbsp; It's around.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>(Granted, there's also a fair bit of Galactus in Obliv's DNA.)</p>",
